WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.360
A security model measured on recall alone.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.267
Aikido published the per-case grid.

00:00:06.267 --> 00:00:08.174
Recall is half a detector.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:14.647
The claim, from Aikido's announcement: Approximately one percentage point less average recall.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:18.892
Altar against its quantised parent, run by run.

00:00:18.892 --> 00:00:22.651
1 of 96: runs that differ, on one case.

00:00:22.651 --> 00:00:25.992
Identical results on 31 of the 32 cases.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.133
Cases in Aikido's CVE benchmark.

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:32.049
32 of 32: with a planted vulnerability.

00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:35.799
No cell for a finding that was not there.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.264
A good compression result, well measured.

00:00:39.264 --> 00:00:42.138
Precision, the deployable half, is not measured.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:49.358
Every number here is from the full article, with its sources, at ai.thesatyajit.com.
